-- הסכם קיבוצי כללי ליישום רפורמת "עוז לתמורה" בחטיבות העליונות (14.8.2011)
-- — the vocabulary its sections share. Only what more than one section
-- uses lives here; a section's own terms live in its own file, beside the
-- clause that coins them.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions

§ `הסכם עוז לתמורה (14.8.2011) — אוצר מילים משותף`

-- The school years the agreement names, each by the calendar year in which
-- it opens on 1 September (convention dates.school-year): תשע"ב is the year
-- from 1.9.2011.
`the school year 5772` MEANS 2011
`the school year 5773` MEANS 2012
`the school year 5774` MEANS 2013
`the school year 5775` MEANS 2014

-- Whether school year y (by the calendar year it opens in) is one of the
-- years from `first` to `last`, both of them in.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, first IS A NUMBER, last IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the school year` y `is from` first `to` last IF
    y AT LEAST first AND y AT MOST last

-- The school years of the reform's part application, תשע"ב–תשע"ד (§5(א)):
-- the only years part ז speaks of.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a year of the Oz part application` y IF
    `the school year` y `is from` `the school year 5772` `to` `the school year 5774`

-- A figure part ז sets for each year of part application, given in the
-- text's order (תשע"ב, תשע"ג, תשע"ד); for any other year it sets none.
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, `in 5772` IS A NUMBER, `in 5773` IS A NUMBER, `in 5774` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `by the year of part application` y `in 5772` `in 5773` `in 5774` IS
    BRANCH
        IF y EQUALS `the school year 5772` THEN JUST `in 5772`
        IF y EQUALS `the school year 5773` THEN JUST `in 5773`
        IF y EQUALS `the school year 5774` THEN JUST `in 5774`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- How far the reform reaches, in a school in a school year (§5(א)) or in
-- the terms a teaching employee is employed on (§§6–8): in full, in part
-- (part ז, in the school years תשע"ב–תשע"ד), or not at all.
DECLARE `extent of the Oz reform` IS ONE OF
    `the Oz reform in full`
    `the Oz reform in part`
    `off the Oz reform`

-- What §§6(ב) and 7(ח) ask of a teaching employee before the reform may
-- reach him, and §5(ב) and §8(ב)(1) through them.
@desc A teaching employee's position and qualifications, as §§6(ב) and 7(ח) ask.
DECLARE `Oz teaching employee's qualifications` HAS
    `position share with the employers, in all` IS A NUMBER  @desc with all the employers together (אצל המעסיקים, במצטבר); 1 is a full position
    `entitled to a permanent teaching licence or a licence to teach` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds an academic degree` IS A BOOLEAN
    `teaches a field with no relevant academic education, with a permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a teaching permit given by the Ministry's instructions
    `holds technological education relevant to the field taught` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN q IS A `Oz teaching employee's qualifications`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds a licence and a degree` q IF
    q's `entitled to a permanent teaching licence or a licence to teach` AND q's `holds an academic degree`

GIVEN q IS A `Oz teaching employee's qualifications`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employed below a third of a position` q IF
    q's `position share with the employers, in all` LESS THAN 1/3

-- The three kinds of hour the Oz work week is made of (§9(ו)).
@desc A teacher's weekly hours in the school under the Oz reform.
DECLARE `Oz work week` HAS
    `frontal teaching hours`       IS A NUMBER @desc in front of a class; role hours that replace them count here (§10(א))
    `individual hours with pupils` IS A NUMBER @desc with a group of up to 3 pupils, or up to 5 (§9(ו)(2))
    `teaching-support hours`       IS A NUMBER @desc in the school, on the work §9(ו)(3) lists

GIVEN w IS A `Oz work week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours of the Oz week` w IS
    w's `frontal teaching hours` PLUS w's `individual hours with pupils` PLUS w's `teaching-support hours`

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER, i IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Oz work week`
DECIDE `an Oz week of` f i s IS
    `Oz work week` WITH
        `frontal teaching hours`       IS f
        `individual hours with pupils` IS i
        `teaching-support hours`       IS s

-- The roles part ד pays and counts, in §17's table's order: סגן מנהל
-- בית ספר, רכז שכבה (י'–י"ב, and ט' in a four-year school), רכז חינוך
-- חברתי, רכז התאמות ללמידה והיבחנות בבחינות הבגרות, רכז מקצוע, רכז מדידה
-- והערכה, מחנך כיתה, יועץ חינוכי, the teacher the principal gives tasks;
-- then רכז טיולים, which §20 adds; any other role a teacher may be given is
-- `another Oz role` (§17(ב)).
@desc A role a teacher under the Oz reform may hold, as §§17 and 20 name them.
DECLARE `Oz role` IS ONE OF
    `the Oz deputy principal`
    `the Oz grade coordinator`
    `the Oz social-education coordinator`
    `the Oz adjustments coordinator`
    `the Oz subject coordinator`
    `the Oz measurement and evaluation coordinator`
    `the Oz homeroom teacher`
    `the Oz educational counsellor`
    `the Oz teacher with tasks the principal assigns`
    `the Oz trips coordinator`
    `another Oz role`

-- What a salary component is "brought into account" for (§16(ב), §20(ז),
-- §38(ג), §39(ב)): the hour value, severance pay under the Severance Pay
-- Law, contributions to a pension provident fund, to a training fund and to
-- the Dafna fund, and computing a percentage supplement on the combined
-- salary — the supplements those sections name by name (the Oz LaTmura
-- supplement among them, which §§38(ג) and 39(ב) keep their supplements
-- out of), the rest (role allowances among them) together.
DECLARE `what an Oz salary component counts for` IS ONE OF
    `computing the hour value`
    `Oz severance pay under the Severance Pay Law`
    `contributions to a pension provident fund`
    `contributions to a training fund`
    `contributions to the Dafna fund`
    `computing supplement 2001`
    `computing supplement 2008`
    `computing the Oz LaTmura supplement`
    `computing supplement 2011`
    `computing erosion supplement 2011`
    `computing the promotion-grade supplement`
    `computing another percentage supplement on the combined salary`

`what an Oz salary component may count for` MEANS
    LIST `computing the hour value`, `Oz severance pay under the Severance Pay Law`, `contributions to a pension provident fund`, `contributions to a training fund`, `contributions to the Dafna fund`, `computing supplement 2001`, `computing supplement 2008`, `computing the Oz LaTmura supplement`, `computing supplement 2011`, `computing erosion supplement 2011`, `computing the promotion-grade supplement`, `computing another percentage supplement on the combined salary`

GIVEN p IS A `what an Oz salary component counts for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `computing a percentage supplement` p IF
        p EQUALS `computing supplement 2001`
    OR p EQUALS `computing supplement 2008`
    OR p EQUALS `computing the Oz LaTmura supplement`
    OR p EQUALS `computing supplement 2011`
    OR p EQUALS `computing erosion supplement 2011`
    OR p EQUALS `computing the promotion-grade supplement`
    OR p EQUALS `computing another percentage supplement on the combined salary`

-- A salary month, counted as twelve to the year so that months compare in
-- order: the salary of August 2012 is `the Oz salary month` 2012 8. "In the
-- salary of month X" is that month itself (convention dates.salary-month).
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Oz salary month` y m IS
    y TIMES 12 PLUS m

-- Part י's one-time grants (§§35–37) are paid "for a teacher employed at
-- 100% of a position" and, to one employed part-time or in part of the
-- school year, in proportion to his position and to the part of the year he
-- was employed; employment beyond a full position does not count (§§35(ג),
-- 36(ה), and §37 through its "100% משרה"). The share of the year each
-- section measures is its own.
GIVEN `the grant for a full position` IS A NUMBER
      `position share` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 is a full position
      `share of the school year` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 is the whole year, as the section measures it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an Oz grant pro rata` `the grant for a full position` `position share` `share of the school year` IS
    `the grant for a full position` TIMES min `position share` 1 TIMES `share of the school year`

-- A teacher in a school year, as part י's one-time grants (§§35–37) ask
-- about him. Months are counted in the school year, which runs September
-- to August (convention dates.school-year); a share of it is the section's
-- to measure.
@desc A teacher in a school year, as the one-time grants of §§35–37 ask about him.
DECLARE `Oz grant teacher` HAS
    `position share` IS A NUMBER @desc his position in the school year; 1 is a full position
    `months employed` IS A NUMBER @desc months of the school year (September to August) he was employed and at work: a month of unpaid leave, sabbatical or maternity leave is not among them
    `months on maternity leave` IS A NUMBER @desc months of the school year on maternity leave under the Women's Employment Law, 1954 (unpaid leave after it not among them)
    `months employed from September to June` IS A NUMBER @desc the months employed, of September to June only
    `months on maternity leave from September to June` IS A NUMBER @desc the months on maternity leave, of September to June only
    `months on unpaid leave or sabbatical` IS A NUMBER @desc months of the school year on unpaid leave (חל"ת) or on sabbatical
    `a substitute only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed by the employer as a substitute only
    `on the reform's terms` IS A `extent of the Oz reform` @desc how far the reform reached him in the school year

-- Part י's grants are updated every June, from June 2012, by the change in
-- the consumer price index between the index published for May before the
-- update and that for May of the year before (§§35(ה), 36(ז)). Each update
-- applies to the amount in force on its day (convention
-- dates.update-in-force), exactly (convention rounding.default): given the
-- May indices in order, from May 2011 to the May before the last update,
-- the amount moves by each year's ratio in turn.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      `the May indices` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc the CPI published for May of each year, from May 2011 to the May before the last update, in order
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an Oz grant updated each June` amount `the May indices` IS
    CONSIDER `the May indices`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN amount
    WHEN earlier FOLLOWED BY later THEN
        CONSIDER later
        WHEN EMPTY THEN amount
        WHEN next FOLLOWED BY rest THEN `an Oz grant updated each June` (amount TIMES next DIVIDED BY earlier) later

#ASSERT `the hours of the Oz week` (`an Oz week of` 24 6 10) EQUALS 40
#ASSERT count (filter `computing a percentage supplement` `what an Oz salary component may count for`) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the school year` 2012 `is from` `the school year 5772` `to` `the school year 5774`
#ASSERT `by the year of part application` `the school year 5773` 1 2 3 EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `by the year of part application` `the school year 5775` 1 2 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `a year of the Oz part application` `the school year 5775`
#ASSERT `the Oz salary month` 2011 9 GREATER THAN `the Oz salary month` 2011 8 AND `the Oz salary month` 2012 1 GREATER THAN `the Oz salary month` 2011 12
#ASSERT `an Oz grant pro rata` 5500 1.2 1 EQUALS 5500 AND `an Oz grant pro rata` 5500 0.5 0.5 EQUALS 1375
-- two updates, by +2% and then +1%: 5,500 × 102/100 × 103.02/102
#ASSERT `an Oz grant updated each June` 5500 (LIST 100, 102, 103.02) EQUALS 5666.1
#ASSERT `an Oz grant updated each June` 5500 (LIST 100) EQUALS 5500 AND `an Oz grant updated each June` 5500 EMPTY EQUALS 5500

§§ `טבלאות שבוע העבודה בנספחים א'–ג'3`

-- Twelve annexes print the Oz week as tables: א'–א'3 a mother's (§§11 and
-- 26(ד)), ב'–ב'3 a teacher's entitled to the full age reduction (§§12 and
-- 26(ד)), ג'–ג'3 a part-time teacher's (§§13 and 26(ב)); the annex without
-- a number is the reform in full, those numbered 1–3 its part application
-- in תשע"ב, תשע"ג and תשע"ד. A table's columns run from the full position
-- down, a frontal hour at a time. Its rows are "היקף משרה", in a mother's
-- table also "היקף משרה אילולא הייתה אם", "שעות פרונטאליות (כולל שעות חינוך
-- שעות הכנה לבגרות ושעות תפקיד אחרות)", "שעות פרטנית", "שעות תומכות הוראה"
-- and "משך הנוכחות השבועית בבית הספר (שעות של 60 דקות)". Each column in the
-- annexes' files is one printed column, its cells in that order, as the
-- corpus publishes them; a cell that departs from its table's pattern stays
-- as printed, and the checks below name it.
@desc One printed column of a work-week table in the Oz agreement's annexes.
DECLARE `Oz annexed column` HAS
    `the position printed`               IS A NUMBER @desc "היקף משרה" as printed; in a mother's table, the position she is paid on
    `the would-have position printed`    IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc "היקף משרה אילולא הייתה אם", printed in a mother's table only
    `the frontal hours printed`          IS A NUMBER @desc with the homeroom, bagrut-preparation and other role hours
    `the individual hours printed`       IS A NUMBER
    `the teaching-support hours printed` IS A NUMBER
    `the presence printed`               IS A NUMBER @desc the weekly presence in the school, in hours of 60 minutes

GIVEN p IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER, i IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER, w IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Oz annexed column`
DECIDE `an Oz annexed column` p f i s w IS
    `Oz annexed column` WITH
        `the position printed`               IS p
        `the would-have position printed`    IS NOTHING
        `the frontal hours printed`          IS f
        `the individual hours printed`       IS i
        `the teaching-support hours printed` IS s
        `the presence printed`               IS w

GIVEN p IS A NUMBER, would IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER, i IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER, w IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Oz annexed column`
DECIDE `an Oz annexed mother's column` p would f i s w IS
    `Oz annexed column` WITH
        `the position printed`               IS p
        `the would-have position printed`    IS JUST would
        `the frontal hours printed`          IS f
        `the individual hours printed`       IS i
        `the teaching-support hours printed` IS s
        `the presence printed`               IS w

-- The ages a table is for, as its caption prints them: none (the teacher
-- under 50), "מגיל 50 עד גיל 55" (or "ועד"), "מעל גיל 55". Which band a
-- teacher is in is the age-reduction rules' (§12): a fact of the case.
@desc The age band an annexed work-week table is for.
DECLARE `Oz annexed age band` IS ONE OF
    `the Oz band under 50`
    `the Oz band from 50 to 55`
    `the Oz band over 55`

`the Oz age bands` MEANS LIST `the Oz band under 50`, `the Oz band from 50 to 55`, `the Oz band over 55`

-- What a table is for: a teacher's week by the position, or a mother's
-- under §11(א) (she cuts her hours) or §11(ב) (she keeps the week she would
-- have had), as the caption's "(א)" or "(ב)" names the sub-section.
@desc What an annexed work-week table is for.
DECLARE `Oz annexed table's use` IS ONE OF
    `the week by the position`
    `a mother cutting her hours, section 11(א)`
    `a mother keeping her week, section 11(ב)`

@desc A work-week table in the Oz agreement's annexes.
DECLARE `Oz annexed table` HAS
    `the annex printing it` IS A STRING
    `the age band it is for` IS AN `Oz annexed age band`
    `what it is for`         IS AN `Oz annexed table's use`
    `its columns`            IS A LIST OF `Oz annexed column`

-- A mother's two tables for one age band (annexes א'–א'3): the (א) table
-- prints the (ב) table's columns cut by one, as the checks below compare.
@desc A mother's two tables for one age band, under §11(א) and under §11(ב).
DECLARE `Oz mother's tables` HAS
    `the table under (א)` IS AN `Oz annexed table`
    `the table under (ב)` IS AN `Oz annexed table`

-- What a table gives a teacher: the week he works, the position he is
-- employed in (for a mother, the one she would have had, which §11(ה)
-- keeps her tenure in) and the position his salary is computed on (larger
-- for a mother, §11(ב) and §26(ה)).
@desc What an annexed work-week table gives a teacher.
DECLARE `Oz annexed week` HAS
    `the week it gives`           IS AN `Oz work week`
    `the position employed in`    IS A NUMBER @desc 1 is a full position
    `the position paid on`        IS A NUMBER @desc 1 is a full position

GIVEN c IS AN `Oz annexed column`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the hours of the annexed column` c IS
    c's `the frontal hours printed` PLUS c's `the individual hours printed` PLUS c's `the teaching-support hours printed`

GIVEN c IS AN `Oz annexed column`
GIVETH AN `Oz work week`
DECIDE `the annexed column's week` c IS
    `an Oz week of` (c's `the frontal hours printed`) (c's `the individual hours printed`) (c's `the teaching-support hours printed`)

-- A table's full position, in hours: the presence its first column prints,
-- the column of a position of 100% (for a mother's table, of the position
-- she would have had). Every table's first column is that position, as the
-- annexes' checks confirm; the sections that send to them hold it to their
-- own full week (§§9(ו), 12 and 26(א)).
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the full position's hours in the annexed table` t IS
    CONSIDER t's `its columns`
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN c's `the presence printed`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0

GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, hours IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the share of the annexed table's full position` t hours IS
    hours DIVIDED BY `the full position's hours in the annexed table` t

-- A position the tables print, to the hundredth of a percent (96.05% is
-- 36.5 of 38 hours), with an exact half going up (convention rounding.half).
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `to the hundredth of a percent` x IS
    x `to the nearest` 0.0001

GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Oz annexed column`
DECIDE `the column the annexed table prints for` t f IS
    listToMaybe (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the frontal hours printed` EQUALS f) (t's `its columns`))

-- The note under every table ("הערה: במקרה בו סך שעות הפרונטאליות ושעות
-- התפקיד ... אינו מספר שלם"): frontal and role hours that are not whole take
-- the individual and support hours of the column whose frontal hours are
-- nearest to them "על פי כללי העיגול" — an exact half going up (convention
-- rounding.half) — and the position is all the hours together over the
-- full position's. Whole hours are a column's own.
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Oz annexed column`
DECIDE `the column the annexes' note takes for` t f IS
    `the column the annexed table prints for` t (`to the nearest whole` f)

GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Oz work week`
DECIDE `the week the annexed table gives` t f IS
    CONSIDER `the column the annexes' note takes for` t f
    WHEN JUST c THEN JUST (`an Oz week of` f (c's `the individual hours printed`) (c's `the teaching-support hours printed`))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- The position of a week: its hours over the full position's. For whole
-- frontal hours it is the column's, to the hundredth of a percent the
-- table prints (convention rounding.printed-figure), and where a printed
-- cell departs from its hours (F-oz-founding-annex-g-a), the hours decide
-- (convention reading.misprint). For hours the note computes it is exact:
-- the note names no rounding (convention rounding.default).
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, w IS AN `Oz work week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position of the week in the annexed table` t w IS
    IF w's `frontal teaching hours` EQUALS FLOOR (w's `frontal teaching hours`)
    THEN `to the hundredth of a percent` share
    ELSE share
    WHERE
        share MEANS `the share of the annexed table's full position` t (`the hours of the Oz week` w)

-- What a table of the week by the position gives a teacher with f frontal
-- and role hours.
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Oz annexed week`
DECIDE `what the annexed table gives for` t f IS
    CONSIDER `the week the annexed table gives` t f
    WHEN JUST w THEN
        LET p MEANS `the position of the week in the annexed table` t w
        IN  JUST (`an Oz annexed week of` w p p)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN w IS AN `Oz work week`, employed IS A NUMBER, paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Oz annexed week`
DECIDE `an Oz annexed week of` w employed paid IS
    `Oz annexed week` WITH
        `the week it gives`        IS w
        `the position employed in` IS employed
        `the position paid on`     IS paid

-- The note under the tables of annexes ב'–ג'3: a teacher with fewer frontal
-- hours (with his homeroom and role hours) than the note names works
-- frontal hours only, at those hours over the full position's. The note
-- divides by "בסיס המשרה ברפורמה": the table's own full position, the
-- reading F-oz-founding-annex-b-a adopts.
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, fewest IS A NUMBER, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Oz annexed week`
DECIDE `what the annexed table gives, frontal hours only below` t fewest f IS
    IF f LESS THAN fewest
    THEN JUST (`an Oz annexed week of` (`an Oz week of` f 0 0) share share)
    ELSE `what the annexed table gives for` t f
    WHERE
        share MEANS `the share of the annexed table's full position` t f

-- §11(ב)'s step in a mother's tables: the points the (ב) table's first
-- column adds to the position she would have had (107.00% over 100.00% in
-- annex א'). §§11(ב) and 26(ה) hold each annex's step to their own rate.
GIVEN m IS AN `Oz mother's tables`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the points the mother's tables add` m IS
    CONSIDER m's `the table under (ב)`'s `its columns`
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN c's `the position printed` MINUS fromMaybe 0 (c's `the would-have position printed`)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0

-- §11(ב): a mother keeping the week she would have had (f frontal and role
-- hours) works its week, is employed in its position and is paid on that
-- position and the annex's step.
GIVEN m IS AN `Oz mother's tables`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Oz annexed week`
DECIDE `what the mother's tables give a mother keeping her week` m f IS
    CONSIDER `the week the annexed table gives` t f
    WHEN JUST w THEN
        LET p MEANS `the position of the week in the annexed table` t w
        IN  JUST (`an Oz annexed week of` w p (p PLUS `the points the mother's tables add` m))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        t MEANS m's `the table under (ב)`

-- §11(א): a mother cutting her hours, whose week would have been the (ב)
-- table's column for f frontal and role hours, works the column after it —
-- one frontal hour less — and is paid on that week's position and the
-- annex's step, her position staying the one she would have had. This is
-- the (א) table as every one of its columns prints it, but those
-- F-oz-founding-annex-a-a names, read by the same pattern (convention
-- reading.consistent). The (ב) table's last column has none after it.
GIVEN m IS AN `Oz mother's tables`, f IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Oz annexed week`
DECIDE `what the mother's tables give a mother cutting her hours` m f IS
    CONSIDER `the column the annexes' note takes for` t f
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST c THEN
        CONSIDER `the column the annexed table prints for` t (c's `the frontal hours printed` MINUS 1)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST next THEN
            LET cut MEANS `an Oz week of` (f MINUS 1) (next's `the individual hours printed`) (next's `the teaching-support hours printed`)
            IN  LET would MEANS `the position of the week in the annexed table` t (`an Oz week of` f (c's `the individual hours printed`) (c's `the teaching-support hours printed`))
                IN  JUST (`an Oz annexed week of` cut would (`the position of the week in the annexed table` t cut PLUS `the points the mother's tables add` m))
    WHERE
        t MEANS m's `the table under (ב)`

-- A table as a finding reads it: the printed table with one column read
-- otherwise (the first column is 1). The printed table stays the data the
-- checks run on; a lookup that must get past the departing cell runs on
-- this.
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, k IS A NUMBER, c IS AN `Oz annexed column`
GIVETH AN `Oz annexed table`
DECIDE `the annexed table with its column` t k `read as` c IS
    `Oz annexed table` WITH
        `the annex printing it`  IS t's `the annex printing it`
        `the age band it is for` IS t's `the age band it is for`
        `what it is for`         IS t's `what it is for`
        `its columns`            IS append (take (k MINUS 1) (t's `its columns`)) (c FOLLOWED BY drop k (t's `its columns`))

-- The checks. A printed cell that departs from its table's pattern is named
-- by its table, its row and its column (the first column is 1), with the
-- figure printed there.
@desc A row of an annexed work-week table.
DECLARE `Oz annexed row` IS ONE OF
    `the position row`
    `the would-have position row`
    `the frontal hours row`
    `the individual hours row`
    `the teaching-support hours row`
    `the presence row`

@desc A printed cell of an annexed table that departs from the table's pattern.
DECLARE `Oz annexed cell` HAS
    `in the annex`  IS A STRING
    `in the band`   IS AN `Oz annexed age band`
    `in the table`  IS AN `Oz annexed table's use`
    `in the row`    IS AN `Oz annexed row`
    `in the column` IS A NUMBER
    `printed there` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, r IS AN `Oz annexed row`, k IS A NUMBER, x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Oz annexed cell`
DECIDE `the cell of` t r k x IS
    `Oz annexed cell` WITH
        `in the annex`  IS t's `the annex printing it`
        `in the band`   IS t's `the age band it is for`
        `in the table`  IS t's `what it is for`
        `in the row`    IS r
        `in the column` IS k
        `printed there` IS x

-- The columns of a table numbered from 1, for the checks.
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`
GIVETH A LIST OF PAIR NUMBER `Oz annexed column`
DECIDE `the numbered columns of` t IS
    zip (range 1 (count (t's `its columns`))) (t's `its columns`)

-- The table's own arithmetic: (1) each column's presence is its hours
-- together, every hour being of 60 minutes (§§9(יא), 26(י)); (2) each
-- position — in a mother's table, the position she would have had — is its
-- hours over the full position's, to the hundredth of a percent. A mother's
-- (א) table is held to its (ב) table instead (below), its positions not
-- being its own hours'.
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, k IS A NUMBER, c IS AN `Oz annexed column`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Oz annexed cell`
DECIDE `the cells of the column off its arithmetic` t k c IS
    append presence position
    WHERE
        presence MEANS
            IF `the hours of the annexed column` c EQUALS c's `the presence printed`
            THEN EMPTY
            ELSE LIST (`the cell of` t `the presence row` k (c's `the presence printed`))
        share MEANS `to the hundredth of a percent` (`the share of the annexed table's full position` t (`the hours of the annexed column` c))
        position MEANS
            IF t's `what it is for` EQUALS `a mother cutting her hours, section 11(א)`
            THEN EMPTY
            ELSE CONSIDER c's `the would-have position printed`
                 WHEN JUST would THEN IF would EQUALS share THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST (`the cell of` t `the would-have position row` k would)
                 WHEN NOTHING THEN IF c's `the position printed` EQUALS share THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST (`the cell of` t `the position row` k (c's `the position printed`))

GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Oz annexed cell`
DECIDE `the cells of the annexed table off its arithmetic` t IS
    concat (map (GIVEN kc YIELD CONSIDER kc WHEN PAIR OF k, c THEN `the cells of the column off its arithmetic` t k c) (`the numbered columns of` t))

-- The columns step down a frontal hour at a time, from the full position.
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annexed table steps down an hour a column` t IF
    all (GIVEN pair YIELD CONSIDER pair WHEN PAIR OF a, b THEN a's `the frontal hours printed` MINUS b's `the frontal hours printed` EQUALS 1)
        (zip (t's `its columns`) (drop 1 (t's `its columns`)))

-- The week of a table's first column, its full position.
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Oz work week`
DECIDE `the week of the annexed table's full position` t IS
    CONSIDER t's `its columns`
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (`the annexed column's week` c)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING

-- The frontal hours of a table's last column: the fewest it prints.
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the frontal hours of the annexed table's last column` t IS
    minimum (map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the frontal hours printed`) (t's `its columns`))

-- The first column is the full position: 100% (in a mother's (ב) table,
-- the position she would have had).
GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annexed table opens at the full position` t IF
    CONSIDER t's `its columns`
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN fromMaybe (c's `the position printed`) (c's `the would-have position printed`) EQUALS 1
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE

-- A mother's tables: (3) in the (ב) table, each position she is paid on is
-- the one she would have had and the annex's step; (4) the (א) table's
-- column k is the (ב) table's column k+1 — the hours she works — with the
-- position she would have had of the (ב) column k, and paid on the (ב)
-- column k+1's position and the step.
GIVEN m IS AN `Oz mother's tables`, c IS AN `Oz annexed column`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the position the mother's tables pay on the column` m c IS
    `to the hundredth of a percent` (`the share of the annexed table's full position` (m's `the table under (ב)`) (`the hours of the annexed column` c))
        PLUS `the points the mother's tables add` m

GIVEN m IS AN `Oz mother's tables`, k IS A NUMBER, c IS AN `Oz annexed column`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Oz annexed cell`
DECIDE `the cells of the (ב) column off the step` m k c IS
    IF c's `the position printed` EQUALS fromMaybe 0 (c's `the would-have position printed`) PLUS `the points the mother's tables add` m
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE LIST (`the cell of` (m's `the table under (ב)`) `the position row` k (c's `the position printed`))

GIVEN t IS AN `Oz annexed table`, r IS AN `Oz annexed row`, k IS A NUMBER, printed IS A NUMBER, pattern IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Oz annexed cell`
DECIDE `the cell if it departs` t r k printed pattern IS
    IF printed EQUALS pattern THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST (`the cell of` t r k printed)

GIVEN m IS AN `Oz mother's tables`, k IS A NUMBER, c IS AN `Oz annexed column`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Oz annexed cell`
DECIDE `the cells of the (א) column off the (ב) table` m k c IS
    CONSIDER `the column the annexed table prints for` b (c's `the frontal hours printed`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST (`the cell of` a `the frontal hours row` k (c's `the frontal hours printed`))
    WHEN JUST twin THEN
        concat (LIST
            `the cell if it departs` a `the individual hours row` k (c's `the individual hours printed`) (twin's `the individual hours printed`),
            `the cell if it departs` a `the teaching-support hours row` k (c's `the teaching-support hours printed`) (twin's `the teaching-support hours printed`),
            `the cell if it departs` a `the would-have position row` k (fromMaybe 0 (c's `the would-have position printed`)) (fromMaybe 0 ((at (b's `its columns`) (k MINUS 1))'s `the would-have position printed`)),
            `the cell if it departs` a `the position row` k (c's `the position printed`) (`the position the mother's tables pay on the column` m twin))
    WHERE
        a MEANS m's `the table under (א)`
        b MEANS m's `the table under (ב)`

GIVEN m IS AN `Oz mother's tables`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Oz annexed cell`
DECIDE `the cells of the mother's tables off their pattern` m IS
    append
        (concat (map (GIVEN kc YIELD CONSIDER kc WHEN PAIR OF k, c THEN `the cells of the (ב) column off the step` m k c) (`the numbered columns of` (m's `the table under (ב)`))))
        (concat (map (GIVEN kc YIELD CONSIDER kc WHEN PAIR OF k, c THEN `the cells of the (א) column off the (ב) table` m k c) (`the numbered columns of` (m's `the table under (א)`))))
